The active sentence emphasizes the subject performing the action, while the passive sentence emphasizes the object receiving the action. Active sentences are often more direct and concise, while passive sentences can be useful when the focus is on the object or when the subject is unknown or unimportant. In general, it is recommended to use active sentences when possible, but passive sentences can be appropriate in certain situations, such as when the object is more important than the subject or when the subject is unknown.

