task_net = fullyConnectedLayer(num_classes);
task_net = softmaxLayer();
task_net = classificationLayer();
% Generate some training data for the animal recognition task
X_train = randn(num_samples, num_features);
y_train = randi(num_classes, num_samples, 1);
% Train the meta-learner neural network on the animal recognition task
meta_learner = trainNetwork(X_train, categorical(y_train), meta_learner);
% Generate some test data for a new animal recognition task
X_test = randn(num_samples, num_features);
y_test = randi(num_classes, num_samples, 1);
% Use the meta-learner to initialize the task-specific neural network
task_net = initializeNetworkWithMetaLearner(X_train, categorical(y_train), meta_learner);
% Fine-tune the task-specific neural network on the new animal recognition task
task_net = trainNetwork(X_test, categorical(y_test), task_net);
```
Note that this is just a simple example and there are many variations of the L2L approach that can be used for different types of tasks.

